M04-M07 FIRST APPLICATION UI WIRING GATES
=======================================
Seven independent Playwright cases in application-workflows.spec.ts visit the
real root App. application-fixture.ts mocks ONLY same-origin HTTP responses;
it does not replace React, routing, controls, file handling or application state.
Run from aspm\web with the existing local browser/dependencies:
  npm.cmd run typecheck
  npm.cmd test -- application-workflows.spec.ts
Compatibility run:
  npm.cmd test -- shell.spec.ts m01-review-regressions.spec.ts
ASPM_WEB_TEST_PORT can isolate this run from another author's server. Playwright
owns/stops Vite and Chromium; no detached process or real backend is required.

Public API authority: tests\acceptance\CONTRACT.txt at repository root.
No backend routes, authorization or persistence are invented by these tests.
All users, memberships, reports, cookie values and setup/password canaries are
explicitly synthetic. Mock success is UI mapping evidence, not real auth/PG/S3
or scanner, live integration, verification, deployment or permission evidence.

Planned auth behavior shift, not a bypass
---------------------------------------
Startup calls GET /api/v1/session before protected requests. A 200 supplies
{apiVersion,user:{id,name,email},workspaces:[{id,name,role}],expiresAt}.
401 shows Sign in without rendering cached findings/assets/details/workspaces.
Use credentials:same-origin and the server's HttpOnly aspm_session cookie;
never Authorization, browser token storage, URL credentials or credential logs.
New cookie fixtures use loopback HTTP and HttpOnly. Production Secure/HTTPS
cookie and server revocation requirements remain in the real backend gates.
The browser suite does not weaken or claim to retest those transport guarantees.

The legacy M01 fixture gains only synthetic GET /api/v1/session and an empty
GET /api/v1/assets response for navigation. Its GET-only credential/network
guards and ALL existing assertions remain unchanged. The new fixture admits
only the explicit writes below. No test-mode flag or fixture import belongs in
production. No provenance/source-approval test or record is changed.

Security-first review and frozen expectations
--------------------------------------------
Prioritize cases 1, 2 and 4: session entry, logout/expiry and scope changes must
remove protected data, including hidden/cached views, before more happy-path
breadth. A workspace header is a selector, not authority. Real application
authorization must bind the authenticated session to server-owned membership,
role and object workspace; hidden controls or client-supplied roles cannot grant
access. Current browser fixtures do NOT prove that enforcement: their admin/
analyst metadata does not exercise real viewer-write denial or role revocation.
Require separate real-application negative authorization evidence.

The next test work is security-negative coverage, not more CRUD/import breadth.
The parent will arrange authorized real storage fixtures for:
  - An owned-object positive control using scoped credentials, plus actual
    storage-service denial for a different prefix and a different bucket.
  - Revocation while a read is deliberately blocked, with a bounded release/
    cancellation and an assertion that no protected data is disclosed afterward.
Keep application authorization, storage credential/policy denial and in-flight
revocation evidence distinct. An app-only 403/prefix check or a mocked storage
error does NOT prove storage isolation. The held Beta response in browser case
4 only checks workspace-switch presentation; it is not a revocation test.
These real security cases are NOT RUN / UNVERIFIED pending the parent's scoped
fixtures. Do not use broad existing fixture credentials as isolation evidence,
copy credential values into this handoff, or modify shared storage policies.

HANDOFF.sha256 records exact-byte SHA-256 hashes of the delivered browser tests,
fixtures, contracts and existing M01 expectation/provenance controls before the
coder handoff. Paths are relative to this tests directory; the manifest excludes
itself. Formatting/line-ending changes also change a hash. The production coder
must not edit expectations or regenerate the baseline to make implementation
pass. Any contract change requires separate independent test-author review.

First accessible workflows
--------------------------
1. Authenticated entry shows a native select/combobox named Workspace whose
   values are membership IDs. Sign out POSTs /api/v1/logout, then unmounts
   protected data/context. Reload must not restore a logged-out view.
2. A form named Sign in has Email and Password labels and a Sign in submit.
   POST /api/v1/login sends {email,password}; password input is masked.
   Invalid credentials show an actionable alert without echoing the password.
   Login's user/workspaces response enters Work with no client-held auth token.
   A later protected 401 (Refresh on Work) clears cached data immediately and
   returns to Sign in; reload remains denied.
3. The unauthenticated entry offers Set up instance for the operator with an
   out-of-band token. This is not automatic bootstrap-state discovery: no such
   discovery endpoint exists in the public contract. The form of that name has
   Workspace name, Name, Email, Password and masked Bootstrap token fields.
   POST /api/v1/bootstrap sends {workspaceName,name,email,password}, with token
   ONLY in X-ASPM-Bootstrap-Token. After 201, show setup success and Sign in.
   This first flow requires explicit login, not implicit session creation.
4. Workspace change updates X-ASPM-Workspace-ID on protected reads/writes and
   clears query, selection, detail and old rows BEFORE the new work response.
   A held Beta response tests this boundary without timing sleeps.
5. Assets has Create asset and a form named Create asset. Labels: Asset name,
   Kind (repository), Environment (text), Criticality (medium/high), Tags
   (comma-separated text). Empty owner maps to ownerId:null.
   POST /api/v1/assets returns the actual asset ID and row in table Assets.
   Its Edit asset button opens Edit asset with populated values; Save asset
   PATCHes /api/v1/assets/{returned-id}. Keep selected workspace and Assets route.
6. Assets offers Import report and a form named Import report. Labels:
   Asset, Format, Report file, Source ID, Scan ID, Scope ID, Scope revision,
   Branch, Source scan time, Source status, Scan kind, Completeness.
   Select controls use API values. Source scan time accepts RFC3339 UTC text;
   blank means null, never now. The client supplies current collectedAt.
   Format values: sarif and generic-json. Report file is a real file input;
   tests select in-memory local File payloads with CRLF/trailing newline bytes.
   POST /api/v1/imports is the ONE JSON wrapper in the backend contract, not
   multipart. Preserve report string bytes and every source/scan/scope field.
   First Generic JSON profile uses literal array-field mapping:
     sourceFindingId=id, title=title, sourceSeverity=severity,
     sourceLocation=path, sourceLine=line, impact=impact,
     remediation=remediation, description=description.
   No mapping scripts or broad format/UI framework are required.
   An accessible status/alert named Import status shows queued/pending after
   202, not success. Refresh import status GETs /api/v1/imports/{returned-id}.
   Display processing, succeeded and failed from responses, including failure
   diagnostics. Optional bounded polling may coexist, but never simulate job
   completion in a UI timer. The JSON fixture deliberately returns a server
   failure despite valid local JSON, so client parsing is not success evidence.
7. Work still uses table Findings, Filter findings and its existing detail
   dialog. In detail, list Observations retains BOTH scan records, source IDs,
   uri:line locations, source warning severity and unmapped source notes.
   Preserve the analyst note, accepted-risk disposition and inferred source
   resolution without changing the human workflow or claiming verified closure.
   The existing Freshness & provenance section exposes separate <time datetime>
   values for source scan, source freshness, collection and import. Keep the
   queue's source-scan <time>; collection/import cannot replace it.
   Evidence remains Not verified / Verification not run.

Limits: 60 API requests per case; all external/undeclared operations fail the
fixture. Missing controls/routes are RED, not skips. Password/setup/session
canaries are checked in DOM, URLs, script-readable cookies, storage and console.
These are first usable forms, not all role-management, import formats, pending
job history, retention, mobile layout or production auth deployment coverage.

Observed RED against the unchanged App, September 15, 2026
---------------------------------------------------------
Typecheck passed. Browser run: 7 new failures, 13 existing M01 passes, 0 skips.
Missing: startup session request, Sign in form, Set up instance action,
Workspace selector, Create asset action, Import report action, observation list.
Combined JSON evidence: web\.artifacts\reports\m01-results.json (repository root).
The failures are missing real UI wiring, not missing browser/backend fixtures.
